WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.467
♪♪

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.901
-I'm in a great mood tonight,

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.133
and I'm just going to start off,
I'm going to tell you,

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:09.067
I threw out all my
Mac Tonight merch.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.901
And I just feel better,
you know?

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.534
It was fun while it lasted.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:13.901
Ha ha. I hate it.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.868
And then you send it to me
and then I show it.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.901
But the reality was,
it just put me in a bad mood.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:22.434
It did not spark joy.
It sparked anxiety and terror.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:25.167
And so I threw it all in
the garbage, and I just feel...

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:27.767
I think you're going to see
the difference today

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:29.934
compared to last week,
which was a little low-energy.

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.133
I think we solved the problem.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:33.067
Anyway, we're just --
We're off and running.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:37.400
You guys, we referenced a post
that Trump wrote on social media

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.367
where he wrote
"The election was stollen,"

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:42.734
but he spelled it
with two L's, "stollen."

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.734
A lot of you joke that --
didn't joke, excuse me.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.868
You pointed out that "stollen,"
maybe he meant "stollen,"

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:53.133
which is sort of like
a German Christmas fruitcake.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.634
You know, maybe he wasn't saying

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:59.267
that the election was full
of lies and inconsistency,

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:06.200
but rather it was full of nuts,
spices, dried candy fruits.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.734
Fair point. We shouldn't
jump to conclusions.

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.701
I acted out Rupert Murdoch

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:15.000
telling someone
to move to the left,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.501
but I gestured to the right.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:21.734
That's actually not a mistake,
because in Australia...

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:24.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.567
I referenced "A Few Good Men,"

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:35.033
and in referencing it,
I said the line,

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:39.133
"You're goddamn right
I ordered the Code Red."

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.000
The actual line is,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.434
"You're goddamn right I did."

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:46.067
Did I know that

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:50.667
and still take artistic license
for the purpose of the joke?

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:53.100
-Wait till
they get a load of me.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:01.968
[ Sighs ]

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.968
When I said play
the Nicholson clip,

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:07.968
I just assumed you'd know
I meant...

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:10.133
"You're goddamn right I did."

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.367
You know what I mean?

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.834
Did I know that

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:19.634
and still take artistic license
for the purpose of the joke?

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:21.767
"You're goddamn right I did."

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:24.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.300
It just doesn't work
with any Nicholson clip.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.100
So I said, "Then play
the Nicholson clip."

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.334
You read that email
and you thought,

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:39.467
"Okay, find a Nicholson clip."

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.501
[ Exhales deeply ]

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:45.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:49.734
I said, "if you ever run
into a samurai"

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.767
in last week's Corrections.

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:53.968
Samurais were abolished in 1870.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:58.067
But you keep telling me
cancel culture is not real.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.400
We were talking about,

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.534
Trump has been workshop
in nicknames for Ron DeSantis,

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.367
and we mentioned "Meatball Ron"

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:12.834
and how much we enjoyed
"Meatball Ron."

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:16.701
And I said, "Why keep why keep
digging when you strike gold?"

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:20.767
Well, I've been told by some
gold-digging professionals,

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:25.067
prospectors,
49ers, if you will,

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.067
women of ill repute,

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:31.801
that once you strike gold,

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:34.801
the last thing you want to do
is stop digging.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:38.367
Like, you want to dig more than
you've ever dug before

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:39.601
once you strike gold.

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:44.901
So you don't just say
"eureka" and run off.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:46.601
You know what? I'm...

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:52.200
...almost 50.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.200
And I think I've...

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.434
come to terms with the fact that

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:59.267
I'm never going to yell
"eureka!"

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:02.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:05.367
When you're a kid, you think
it's going to happen.

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:06.634
One day,
you're going to find a thing

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:09.601
or come up with an idea,

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:12.167
gonna scream, "eureka!"

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.534
I can't even imagine
what that would be.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:20.267
Archimedes.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:23.234
Um...

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:25.200
BDSM.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.501
I guess I said it where I put
too much emphasis on the "D."

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:32.234
Maybe that's just
my favorite part.

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:35.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.601
You think a guy
who willingly submits himself

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:42.834
to 75 episodes of "Corrections"
doesn't like a little D?

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.868
We showed a Lego
horse head in bed.

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.868
This is in reference
to how I get bullied

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.634
by the Lego community,

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:01.133
and that because
I accidentally have said

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.801
"Legos" in the past.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:05.334
By way of intimidation,

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:09.167
they put a Lego horse head
in my bed.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:14.200
Well, when you mention "Lego,"
that community has a lot to say.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.234
And I'd love to read
everything they wrote

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:19.300
about our Lego
horse head graphic,

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.701
but I think based on the volume,
it might just be easier

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:25.868
to release it in
3 to 5 coffee table books.

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:31.934
My favorite comment was
someone wrote,

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:34.701
"Lego horse heads don't detach."

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:38.434
Yeah, neither do regular
horses heads.

00:05:38.434 --> 00:05:42.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:45.834
That doesn't stop the mafia
from doing it.

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:49.234
"I want you to put
the Lego horse head

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:51.200
in the Hollywood
producer's bed."

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:55.534
"Only problem is, boss,
they don't come off.

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:58.200
And they sure as hell
ain't gonna go back on.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.901
I just don't think you've
thought it through, boss."

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:11.734
Oh, so at the end
of each "Closer Look,"

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:14.367
What we'll do is we will
call back a clip

00:06:14.367 --> 00:06:16.200
from earlier in
the "Closer Look"

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:21.000
as the final moment
in in the "Closer Look."

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.100
It's a device known in these
parts as "Sal's gambit,"

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.834
and...

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:29.868
at the end of
"A Closer Look" this week,

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:32.000
I said, you know,
Republican voters have a choice

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.868
between a regular D
who has tanked two elections

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:37.334
or a tiny D,
another new nickname

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:39.267
Trump has for Ron DeSantis.

00:06:39.267 --> 00:06:42.100
I'm telling a lot of you this
because I've started to realize

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.133
I don't think a lot of you
are watching the show.

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:47.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:51.200
Or a tiny D that's
not bigger than...

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.167
We cut then to Donald Trump,

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.734
who earlier in the body
of "A Closer Look"

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:57.534
had said in a clip,
"six inches."

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.033
So we said, or a tiny D

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:00.567
that's not bigger
than six inches.

00:07:00.567 --> 00:07:01.801
Well, whew!

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:08.868
The YouTube wires
were clogged with complaints,

00:07:08.868 --> 00:07:11.000
of what I'm going to I'm going
to jump to a conclusion

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.300
and say are gentlemen jackals.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:18.667
Who sent me many, like --

00:07:18.667 --> 00:07:23.968
a lot of data,
a lot of medical charts.

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:29.400
Six inches is average
or above average.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.100
Sometimes you can just tell,
it's not like it's in all-caps,

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:35.100
you can just tell
how fast it was typed.

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:38.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:46.968
A human year being equivalent
to seven dog years is outdated,

00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:48.467
we've been told.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:49.667
That science is outdated.

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:53.033
According to
the American Kennel Club,

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:55.334
the correct answer
when someone asks

00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:57.033
the age of your dog is,

00:07:57.033 --> 00:08:00.100
"What the [bleep] do you care?

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:09.000
Do we have nothing better
to talk about?"

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:18.100
We had a photo of a magician.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.334
Um, someone wrote a correction,

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:25.667
"That's not how magic works,
just loose cards

00:08:25.667 --> 00:08:27.334
in your sleeves."

00:08:27.334 --> 00:08:30.734
Well, correction for you.
It's not magic.

00:08:30.734 --> 00:08:32.033
It's just tricks.

00:08:32.033 --> 00:08:33.801
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:36.267
"That's not how magic works."

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:41.000
Whew.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.901
Big mistake. This is one...

00:08:42.901 --> 00:08:44.868
I mean, this is where
it's actually healthy

00:08:44.868 --> 00:08:46.400
and helpful
that we're doing corrections.

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:50.467
The bear in "Cocaine Bear"
is a woman.

00:08:50.467 --> 00:08:52.634
I got that wrong.

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:56.534
Maybe my favorite comment
I've ever read in "Corrections,"

00:08:56.534 --> 00:08:59.767
"I can't believe you
misgendered Cocaine Bear

00:08:59.767 --> 00:09:02.100
on International Women's Day."

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.033
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.667 --> 00:09:07.901
I mean, if that --

00:09:07.901 --> 00:09:12.701
if that's how I go down,
I apologize.

00:09:12.701 --> 00:09:16.367
A female bear is just as capable

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:19.801
of going on
a drug-filled rampage

00:09:19.801 --> 00:09:21.100
as a male bear

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:25.167
and should be compensated
the same.

00:09:25.167 --> 00:09:28.200
Cocaine Bear, though,

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.200
because she was female,

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.868
broke a 40-year-old
Hollywood record --

00:09:31.868 --> 00:09:35.968
most cocaine
done by an actress on screen,

00:09:35.968 --> 00:09:39.200
formerly held by
Michelle Pfeiffer in "Scarface."

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:43.501
40 years. What a run.

00:09:43.501 --> 00:09:44.868
You don't tighten a gasket.

00:09:44.868 --> 00:09:47.334
You tighten the bolt or nut
that holds the gasket.

00:09:47.334 --> 00:09:48.767
You also don't call Seth Meyers

00:09:48.767 --> 00:09:51.501
when you need a handyman.

00:09:51.501 --> 00:09:53.634
Did you, uh,
try tightening the gasket?

00:09:53.634 --> 00:09:55.868
Get the [bleep]...

00:09:55.868 --> 00:09:58.434
The dog who played Eddie died
before "Frasier" ended,

00:09:58.434 --> 00:10:01.968
which was for the best,
because he always said that if

00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:04.934
Niles and Daphne got together,
the show would jump the shark.

00:10:04.934 --> 00:10:06.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.801 --> 00:10:08.334
Eddie was played by Moose

00:10:08.334 --> 00:10:10.934
and was replaced
on the show "Frasier"

00:10:10.934 --> 00:10:15.901
by his own son, Enzo,
and to this day,

00:10:15.901 --> 00:10:18.334
a lot of suspicions surround...

00:10:20.934 --> 00:10:23.300
Like, where was Enzo?

00:10:27.901 --> 00:10:29.434
Hey, you guys,

00:10:29.434 --> 00:10:32.501
Now is as good a time
to remind you

00:10:32.501 --> 00:10:34.434
that "Corrections"
is twice Emmy-nominated,

00:10:34.434 --> 00:10:36.000
and you just can't
take that away, right?

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:40.300
No matter how bad it gets,
we get to say that forever.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.400
I've been told both times --
we've never won,

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:43.901
but we have finished second
both times,

00:10:43.901 --> 00:10:45.767
I've been told
by trusted sources,

00:10:45.767 --> 00:10:46.834
someone I believe.

00:10:46.834 --> 00:10:47.868
I'm not going to name names.

00:10:47.868 --> 00:10:49.667
He used to be a mayor
of New York,

00:10:49.667 --> 00:10:53.334
hosted "SNL,"
and he told me, finished twice.

00:10:55.567 --> 00:10:56.968
Hey, but you might
not know this.

00:10:56.968 --> 00:10:59.868
We have to pick an episode
to submit that Emmy voters --

00:10:59.868 --> 00:11:01.000
The way it works is, we pick

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.367
what we think is
the best "Corrections."

00:11:02.367 --> 00:11:04.901
We submit it,
Emmy voters receive a link.

00:11:04.901 --> 00:11:06.801
Then the nominees are chosen

00:11:06.801 --> 00:11:10.367
and then those links are sent
to the voters at large,

00:11:10.367 --> 00:11:12.267
and then "Carpool Karaoke" wins.

00:11:12.267 --> 00:11:14.334
And so it's
an interesting process.

00:11:14.334 --> 00:11:17.300
[ Laughter ]

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:20.000
But you know,
there's a very crowdsourced

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.701
piece of of comedy,
of content, you could say.

00:11:22.701 --> 00:11:25.434
"Content" some weeks, you know,

00:11:25.434 --> 00:11:28.801
and every now and then we peek
our head into comedy.

00:11:28.801 --> 00:11:31.667
So we're going to post, if we
can post on Sea Captain Polls,

00:11:31.667 --> 00:11:33.901
and we'll put
Sea Captain Polls down here.

00:11:33.901 --> 00:11:35.300
We would like your input.

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:37.601
What is the best episode
of "Corrections"

00:11:37.601 --> 00:11:38.801
in this Emmy window?

00:11:38.801 --> 00:11:41.801
Which means it has
to be episode 49 or later.

00:11:41.801 --> 00:11:45.601
We genuinely,
you know, obviously,

00:11:45.601 --> 00:11:46.934
there's still a lot
more time to go

00:11:46.934 --> 00:11:48.734
and I obviously
would love to think

00:11:48.734 --> 00:11:52.367
that our best "Corrections"
are ahead of us, you know?

00:11:52.367 --> 00:11:55.667
Obviously not today,
but maybe next week.

00:11:55.667 --> 00:11:57.100
And yeah, so we're
going to post that,

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:59.434
and let us know which is your
favorite one because, again,

00:11:59.434 --> 00:12:04.734
sometimes you strike gold and
keep digging with your jackals.

00:12:04.734 --> 00:12:07.701
And this was my favorite comment
from a jackal this week.

00:12:07.701 --> 00:12:12.467
You know, we had a joke about
the people who sell bags,

00:12:12.467 --> 00:12:16.200
fake designer handbags
in Times Square,

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.400
and they'll sometimes
have a letter off.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:22.334
And we had a bit
about a Hermes bag

00:12:22.334 --> 00:12:26.634
that was spelled with a P
so it would spell "herpes,"

00:12:26.634 --> 00:12:29.667
but they would say
it's a "Herpes" bag.

00:12:29.667 --> 00:12:31.667
And someone said,
you missed the joke,

00:12:31.667 --> 00:12:35.801
which was the tagline
for herpes bag would be,

00:12:35.801 --> 00:12:37.167
"Herpes,

00:12:37.167 --> 00:12:39.167
you'll carry it
with you forever."

00:12:39.167 --> 00:12:41.801
[ Laughter ]

00:12:43.901 --> 00:12:45.067
Not bad.

00:12:45.067 --> 00:12:48.634
Oh, a genuine correction.

00:12:48.634 --> 00:12:51.567
I was told "hearing impaired"
is an outdated term.

00:12:51.567 --> 00:12:53.501
"Deaf and hard of hearing"
are preferred.

00:12:53.501 --> 00:12:55.334
Apologies.

00:12:55.334 --> 00:12:58.200
Learning is what we did
set out to do.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.334
And thank you for telling me
that so politely.

00:13:00.334 --> 00:13:02.767
That is something
I'm very sorry I got wrong.

00:13:02.767 --> 00:13:05.400
Oh, I was also --
This is an interesting point.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:06.567
I don't know
if it's true or not.

00:13:06.567 --> 00:13:09.067
We should keep an eye on it,
because we did --

00:13:09.067 --> 00:13:10.300
and I appreciate
the speed of it --

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:13.601
we now have numbered
episodes in "Corrections."

00:13:13.601 --> 00:13:15.467
Someone said
by numbering our episodes,

00:13:15.467 --> 00:13:18.200
we might be punished
by the YouTube algorithm.

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:20.334
With that said,

00:13:20.334 --> 00:13:22.667
if you've never watched
one of these and then

00:13:22.667 --> 00:13:24.934
it shows up
in your feed one day,

00:13:24.934 --> 00:13:28.801
I would say that's an example
of the algorithm punishing you.

00:13:28.801 --> 00:13:31.767
[ Laughter ]

00:13:31.767 --> 00:13:36.334
I said meth is...

00:13:38.567 --> 00:13:41.000
..."poor man's Ozempic." Ha ha.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.200
But someone said,
you know, for years,

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:45.934
meth was prescribed
for weight loss.

00:13:45.934 --> 00:13:49.367
In fact, amphetamines
obviously prescribed.

00:13:49.367 --> 00:13:54.234
The original "Breaking Bad"
was about a chemistry teacher

00:13:54.234 --> 00:13:57.467
and his former student who
developed a weight loss pill.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:03.000
Breaking "Fat." It's allowed.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.567
Weird Al did it.

00:14:08.501 --> 00:14:10.901
They did? What?
I can't say we...?

00:14:10.901 --> 00:14:12.968
We're nominated for two Emmys?

00:14:12.968 --> 00:14:14.267
They took it away?

00:14:14.801 --> 00:14:17.667
[ Laughter ]

00:14:17.667 --> 00:14:19.767
Oh, speaking of
that YouTube playlist,

00:14:19.767 --> 00:14:21.334
because the first one is --

00:14:21.334 --> 00:14:24.267
well, this week
will be Episode 75.

00:14:24.267 --> 00:14:25.467
Some people were upset.

00:14:25.467 --> 00:14:28.167
They want the playlist
to say Episode 1 first

00:14:28.167 --> 00:14:29.400
so they can click it

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.501
and then it will just autoplay
to the next one,

00:14:31.501 --> 00:14:35.067
because now you have to go
to the bottom and click 1,

00:14:35.067 --> 00:14:37.834
and then when it's over,
you have to click 2.

00:14:37.834 --> 00:14:39.567
We're going to consider
making that change,

00:14:39.567 --> 00:14:41.234
because the last thing
we want any of you to do

00:14:41.234 --> 00:14:44.033
is make
the bare minimum of effort.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:46.634
[ Laughter ]

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.501
[ Laughter ]

00:14:55.934 --> 00:14:58.367
Well, that felt good.

00:14:58.367 --> 00:15:02.667
Tonight felt great, lighter.
More fun.

00:15:02.667 --> 00:15:03.767
Like I felt the change.

00:15:03.767 --> 00:15:05.033
[ Ominous music playing ]

00:15:05.033 --> 00:15:07.634
I don't know if you guys
felt the change, but for me,

00:15:07.634 --> 00:15:09.601
it's just like, better now.

00:15:09.601 --> 00:15:13.234
And I feel like
by getting rid of that stuff,

00:15:13.234 --> 00:15:14.267
the situation --

00:15:14.267 --> 00:15:16.801
-You're goddamn right I did!

00:15:16.801 --> 00:15:19.133
-No, that...!

00:15:19.133 --> 00:15:22.334
That was, "Wait till
they get a load of me."

00:15:22.334 --> 00:15:24.801
[ Laughter ]

00:15:30.534 --> 00:15:31.634
I don't even... What?

